      "message": "This is incorrect coding.\n\nFirst if the `tokenParts.length \u003d\u003d 1` then we have only one element with the index `0`, accessing `tokenParts[1]` will throw an `IndexOutOfBoundsException`.\n\nSecond, the `token.split(\":\", 1)` doesn\u0027t produce the assumed output:\n```\njshell\u003e \"id:token\".split(\":\", 1)\n$8 \u003d\u003d\u003e String[1] { \"id:token\" }\n```\n\nThe Java\u0027s standard `String.split` is bad, see [1]. This is why in Gerrit code\nwe prefer to use Guava `Splitter`:\n```\nList\u003cString\u003e parts \u003d Splitter.on(\":\").splitToList(token);\n```\n\nWe can also add `.trimResults()` on the Splitter creation if we want to be more forgiving about the whitespace that the user may type, like `--token \"id : token\"`\n```\nList\u003cString\u003e parts \u003d Splitter.on(\":\").trimResults().splitToList(token);\n```\n\n[1] https://github.com/google/guava/wiki/StringsExplained#splitter",
